{
  "content": "Hypothesis: to prevent protection status from depending on evaluation order, fade_stale() must snapshot all current TARGET protections at the start of each pass and apply retirement only to claims whose protection status was false at snapshot time; any newly created DEPENDS_ON/CONTRADICTS relations during the pass cannot confer retroactive protection until the next cycle.",
  "scope": {
    "topic": "kernel_design",
    "subtopic": "fade_stale"
  },
  "evidence_class": "INFERRED",
  "kind": "HYPOTHESIS",
  "falsification_test": "Implement two variants (snapshot vs live) on a test substrate containing a chain A DEPENDS_ON B DEPENDS_ON C; retire A mid-pass and observe whether C loses protection within the same pass under live evaluation but retains it under snapshot evaluation.",
  "relation": {
    "target_claim_id": "claim_ed4921b8",
    "relation_type": "DEPENDS_ON",
    "rationale": "directly addresses the timing instability and dangling-reference alternatives raised in the open question"
  }
}
